WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.779
In today's video we'll talk about thermobaric
weapons and their effects on humans but i

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:09.420
make a premise, I am not an expert and I can
t replace those who have made the study of

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.610
certain topics a profession but I can still
make myself useful: translate into simple

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:21.060
words, where possible, complex concepts. Let's
start. On March 1, 2022 a senior US defense

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.170
official tells journalists the deployment,
without specifying the exact location, of

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:32.360
Tos-1 weapon systems capable of sending thermobaric
rockets against Ukrainian targets. A dramatic

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.910
signal dictated by the Russian need to close
the game as quickly as possible, after the

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:42.170
Ukrainians have demonstrated a great ability
to resist to a more numerous and better equipped

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:47.190
enemy. Then the visual confirmation, on the
web are circulating the first videos and images

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:53.100
that show some Russian convoys carrying these
lethal weapons. But what exactly is a thermobaric

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.930
weapon and on what occasions has it been used
throughout history? It is not easy to give

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:02.611
a definition, above all because the term has
been improperly used to include in a single

00:01:02.611 --> 00:01:08.550
category different weapon systems and to describe
different effects. Etymology comes to our

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:14.030
rescue: the Greek words "thermos" and "baros",
respectively heat and pressure, describe well

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:19.461
the effects of these weapons: very high temperature
and dynamic overpressure (or shockwave). In

00:01:19.461 --> 00:01:24.810
the simplest terms, a thermobaric munition
is a type of enhanced explosive munition that

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.159
produces the typical effect of a conventional
high-temperature explosion but, by consuming

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:35.480
the oxygen present in the air, creates a much
greater shockwave, thus increasing the lethality

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:41.370
zone and going to hit victims who are located
further away from the epicenter of the detonation.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:47.500
I open and close a parenthesis: thermobaric
weapon and fuel-air weapon are not synonymous,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:53.600
they are two species of the same genre "enhanced-blast
weapons", because their operating principle

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.060
is different but the effects are the same.
A typical thermobaric device consists of a

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.690
container of a fuel mixture that houses a
small explosive burst charge, called "dispersal

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:09.819
charge." After the mixture is dispersed as
a cloud and mixes with the surrounding oxygen,

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:14.870
the charge causes it to ignite, creating a
large shockwave that does enormous damage,

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:20.060
literally crushing personnel in the immediate
vicinity to death. According to a 1993 study

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.319
by the U.S. Defense Intelligence Agency, the
methods of killing against living targets

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:30.630
are diverse and brutal: what kills is obviously
the pressure wave and subsequent vacuum of

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.990
oxygen, which collapses the lungs, but the
victims will also be severely burned and likely

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:41.380
to breathe in the burning toxic fuel. The
same agency in another paper speculates that

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:46.320
because "the shock and pressure waves cause
minimal damage to brain tissue, it s possible

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:51.490
that victims are not rendered unconscious
by the blast, but instead suffer for several

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:56.209
seconds or minutes while they suffocate."
But it doesn't end there: outside the area

00:02:56.209 --> 00:03:00.910
of the cloud, the shock wave travels very
fast and can hit even those who are beyond

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:05.610
the range of the explosion, causing them serious
injuries to internal organs. Think that the

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.720
pressure that is created is up to 2 times
greater than that generated by a conventional

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.081
explosive weapon. This is confirmed by a study
of the Central Intelligence Agency of the

00:03:15.081 --> 00:03:20.530
United States, for which "the effect of such
an explosion in confined spaces is immense.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:25.569
Those near the ignition point are obliterated.
Those at the fringe are likely to suffer many

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:30.410
internal, and thus invisible injuries . In
addition to collapsing lungs, there is talk

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:36.020
of embolisms in blood vessels, bleeding and
lacerations that can lead to peritonitis,

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:41.170
ruptured eardrums and displacement of eyes
from their sockets. It s not an exaggeration

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:46.610
to say that such devices can have the effects
of a tactical nuclear weapon without the disadvantage

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:52.070
of producing radiations. Because of the mixture's
ability to easily creep into any cavity, there

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:57.489
is nothing that can protect against its devastating
effects, neither natural terrain features

00:03:57.489 --> 00:04:03.129
nor field fortifications that aren t hermetically
sealed. Indeed, the ideal use is precisely

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:08.030
against enclosed structures, such as bunkers
or buildings, since the cloud, by sucking

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:13.239
in materials nearby to fill the oxygen void,
amplifies the destruction of the structure's

00:04:13.239 --> 00:04:18.180
load-bearing elements. As reported by a Russian
military scientist writing for the military

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.740
magazine Voyennyye Znaniya (Military Knowledge),
thermobaric weapons are also effective in

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:28.389
eliminating minefields and completely destroying
the vegetation of a certain area to make room

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:33.569
for helicopter landing sites. In fact, the
US first experimented with this system in

00:04:33.569 --> 00:04:40.080
the 1960s in Vietnam with the famous and massive
daisy-cutter bomb, capable of clearing entire

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.629
sections of forest. In general, the category
of enhanced explosive weapons has found use

00:04:45.629 --> 00:04:52.509
on several occasions: the US used them in
1991 during the first Gulf War, then in 2001

00:04:52.509 --> 00:04:57.490
in Afghanistan in an attempt to flush out
Al-Qaeda members sheltering in the mountains

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:04.330
of Tora Bora, and more recently in 2017 against
ISIL members in the Afghan region of Nangarhar.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:10.360
The Russians, on the other hand, tested several
thermobaric systems in 1969 during the border

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:15.120
conflict with China, then it was the turn
of attacks on the Afghan Panshjir valley in

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.610
the early 1980s against Massoud's forces and
more recently, as Interfax reported, between

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:27.689
October and December 1999 during the offensive
against Chechen forces in the direction of

00:05:27.689 --> 00:05:32.770
the capital Groznyj. During the Russian advance
to take the city, two main thermobaric launch

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:38.050
systems were used: the devastating Tos-1,
also called "Buratino", which we hear so much

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:43.529
about these days, operational since the early
80's during the Soviet-Afghan war and developed

00:05:43.529 --> 00:05:49.949
by the Transmash design office in Omsk. It
s a 220 mm multiple rocket launcher system

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:57.169
mounted on a T-72 tank chassis. Its maximum
effective range is 3.5 km but other sources

00:05:57.169 --> 00:06:03.309
say it could reach 5 km. The other Afghanistan
veteran, much smaller in size clearly, is

00:06:03.309 --> 00:06:09.479
the single-shot RPO-A Shmel shoulder-mounted
launcher with a claimed maximum range of 1km

00:06:09.479 --> 00:06:15.839
and a maximum effective range of 600 m. This
type of weapon is at its best when used as

00:06:15.839 --> 00:06:21.129
a "bunker buster" and loses some effectiveness
when used against dispersed troops in the

00:06:21.129 --> 00:06:26.180
open field, normally killing no more than
a couple in bursts. When used against armored

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:30.879
vehicles, however, it usually damages the
vehicle, but the crew survives and is able

00:06:30.879 --> 00:06:35.729
to return fire. To conclude, it remains to
be understood if there are international treaties

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:41.889
that prohibit or limit the production or use
of such weapons. Unfortunately not, but this

00:06:41.889 --> 00:06:47.259
doesn t mean that there are no arguments against
their development: as reported by Human Rights

00:06:47.259 --> 00:06:52.860
watch, since the enhanced blast weapons cover
a very large area, they are prone to indiscriminate

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:58.490
use, especially in or near populated areas.
In urban settings it s very difficult to direct

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:03.249
the effect of these weapons only to militaries
without involving civilians, because of their

00:07:03.249 --> 00:07:09.229
very nature, and then for the fact that covering
every corner or cr vis make it virtually impossible

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:14.759
for civilians to take shelter from their destructive
effect. So even if a thermobaric weapon is

00:07:14.759 --> 00:07:20.080
aimed at a military target, its extensive
and uncontrollable effect doesn t exclude

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:24.679
the involvement of civilian victims and this,
that is the use of weapons in attacks that

00:07:24.679 --> 00:07:29.969
can not distinguish between combatants and
civilians, is prohibited by the Geneva Conventions

00:07:29.969 --> 00:07:36.460
of 1899 and 1907. However, efforts have not
yet produced concrete results, given that

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:41.039
the 1980 Convention prohibiting the production
of certain conventional weapons deals with

00:07:41.039 --> 00:07:46.009
incendiary weapons, in which category, however,
thermobaric weapons would not fall. And if

00:07:46.009 --> 00:07:51.099
we look at the current conflict between Russia
and Ukraine, the problem doesn t only concern

00:07:51.099 --> 00:07:56.409
the possible use of these weapons but also
of the so-called cluster munitions and obviously

00:07:56.409 --> 00:08:01.999
of the feared nuclear warheads. Some suspect
that Russia has already used the former, despite

00:08:01.999 --> 00:08:07.440
the existence of an international convention
of 2008 that prohibits them and that Moscow,

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:12.869
although not a signatory, has always respected.
The possible use of the Russian nuclear arsenal

00:08:12.869 --> 00:08:18.559
instead, which now counts almost 6000 warheads,
is certainly the most worrying, given the

00:08:18.559 --> 00:08:23.849
recent threats of President Putin to use them,
if any power should interfere militarily.

00:08:23.849 --> 00:08:27.659
Well, we we are done for today, I thank you
all for your attention and see you in the

00:08:27.659 --> 00:08:28.649
next episode. Ciao!

